id: pm-web-g6ac
title: Run the test suite against TypeScript sources behind an uncheatable coverage gate
description: ""
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-28T23:45:37.207Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T01:32:31.345Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T23:47:28.639Z"
author: pi-agent
resolution: "Implemented coverage gate per fleet recipe. Baseline measured at 49.54/80.65/44.83 (line/branch/function) across 26 source files. Thresholds pinned at floor: 49/80/44."
actual_result: "Local gates pass (check, coverage, audit, pack:dry-run, changelog:check). CI legs on Node 22 and 26 are unobserved until the PR runs."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T23:47:14.780Z",pi-agent,"Negative control: created src/__probe.ts exporting one unused function, ran node scripts/coverage-gate.ts — exit code 1, and the gate named src/__probe.ts as never loaded. Deleted the probe and re-ran the gate — exit code 0. The source-presence reconciliation is confirmed not vacuous."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T00:23:41.063Z",claude-code,"Re-verified after the gate was brought to its final form (TZ pinning, build:test chained into the coverage script, tsconfig.test.json rootDir override, and dynamic source-directory walk in place of a frozen file list). Thresholds re-measured against the corrected gate: 49 line, 80 branch, 44 function across 26 source files. Negative control re-run: a throwaway untested file under src makes the gate exit 1 and name it, and it exits 0 again once removed. npm run release:check passes end to end."
  "2026-07-29T01:32:31.345Z",claude-code,"Review round on PR 72 surfaced two defects the gate itself could not catch. First, tsconfig.test.json had been written as a standalone config with strict false and noImplicitAny false, so bringing the test tree into the gated path was typechecking it without strict mode - the opposite of the intent. It now extends the base config, and enabling strict immediately surfaced a real error: resolveLocale in public/src/i18n.ts documents that an explicit null skips a source, and accepts null at runtime, but typed navLang as string only while typing storage as Storage or null. Both the source contract and the test-local declaration now say string or null. Second, the server-entrypoint smoke test placed assert.fail inside a try whose own catch then swallowed it, so a server that started cleanly, or a run that timed out with no numeric status, satisfied the loose status check - the test could not fail. It now captures the outcome and asserts clean-start is false, that the child reported a numeric code, and that the code is non-zero."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T23:47:22.736Z",pi-agent,"Node omits files that never load from its coverage report entirely, rather than reporting them at zero. A bare --test-coverage-lines flag is therefore satisfiable by narrowing what the suite imports. The coverage-gate.ts script reconciles the reported file list against a walk of the source tree to turn that silent omission into a failure naming the missing files. Additionally, Node's strip-only mode does not support TypeScript parameter properties (constructor(public readonly x: string)) — these must be refactored to explicit field declarations. Subprocess V8 coverage IS aggregated by the test runner, so spawning an entrypoint as a subprocess contributes its coverage to the report."
close_reason: "Coverage gate rolled out: tests now import TypeScript sources directly, scripts/coverage-gate.ts enforces per-dimension thresholds plus source-presence reconciliation. All 169 tests pass, negative control confirmed exit 1 with probe and exit 0 without. Gates (npm run check, npm run release:check) pass locally. Two source files refactored to remove parameter properties for Node strip-only compatibility. Server entrypoint exercised via subprocess test."
body: "Coverage was unmeasured here. Tests imported the compiled output from dist/, so the only numbers obtainable pointed at generated JavaScript offsets rather than lines an author edits, and no threshold was wired into any gate.\n\nTests now import the TypeScript sources directly. Node strips types without a flag since 22.18.0, which is the floor this package already declares in engines, so this needs no new tooling. Enabling rewriteRelativeImportExtensions lets a source file import its siblings as ./x.ts while tsc still emits ./x.js into dist, leaving the published artifact's module graph unchanged.\n\nTwo source files used TypeScript parameter properties (constructor(public readonly ...)), which Node's strip-only mode cannot handle. These were refactored to explicit field declarations so the sources run directly under Node without a compiler.\n\nThe server entrypoint (src/server.ts) cannot be imported without side effects — it starts an HTTP server and requires a database. A test was added that spawns it as a subprocess without DATABASE_URL, asserting it exits non-zero, which makes the entrypoint contribute coverage through Node's subprocess V8 coverage aggregation.\n\nThe gate (scripts/coverage-gate.ts) enforces per-dimension thresholds AND reconciles the reported file list against a walk of the source tree. That second check is the reason it is a script rather than a bare flag: Node omits files that never load from its coverage report entirely instead of reporting them at zero.\n\nBaseline across 26 source files (line % / branch % / function %):\n- app.ts: 92.49 / 80.00 / 90.91\n- auth.ts: 70.00 / 40.00 / 75.00\n- board.ts: 98.59 / 88.46 / 100.00\n- crypto.ts: 17.65 / 100.00 / 0.00\n- db.ts: 30.11 / 33.33 / 66.67\n- ical.ts: 100.00 / 91.38 / 100.00\n- index.ts: 42.83 / 93.55 / 26.32\n- middleware/auth.ts: 75.00 / 50.00 / 100.00\n- oidc.ts: 91.78 / 76.99 / 95.83\n- routes/admin.ts: 18.34 / 100.00 / 0.00\n- routes/auth.ts: 21.64 / 100.00 / 0.00\n- routes/extensions.ts: 85.06 / 63.16 / 100.00\n- routes/github.ts: 15.32 / 100.00 / 0.00\n- routes/groups.ts: 15.95 / 100.00 / 0.00\n- routes/oidc.ts: 34.67 / 100.00 / 22.22\n- routes/pm.ts: 23.78 / 76.79 / 7.08\n- routes/projects.ts: 35.23 / 100.00 / 16.67\n- routes/route-params.ts: 100.00 / 50.00 / 100.00\n- routes/sharing.ts: 14.93 / 100.00 / 0.00\n- server.ts: 42.31 / 33.33 / 0.00\n- services/mutation-event-watcher.ts: 99.56 / 85.42 / 76.92\n- services/package-catalog.ts: 100.00 / 100.00 / 100.00\n- services/pm-runner.ts: 79.90 / 76.11 / 71.43\n- services/project-watcher.ts: 93.07 / 82.81 / 80.00\n- services/realtime-bus.ts: 37.20 / 90.91 / 80.00\n- services/sse.ts: 84.86 / 93.33 / 73.91\n\nAggregate: 49.54 line / 80.65 branch / 44.83 function.\nThresholds pinned at floor: 49 / 80 / 44."
